Z||000008||Dave85||08-15-99||08:28 PM||||Just food for thought. I worked 6 yrs. at the worlds leading steel cord plant. We made steel cord for many tire plants and Goodyear has by far the toughest specs. I know it's not saying much about traction but I can tell you they are made better than most.   
Z||000009||ezsurf||08-16-99||11:00 AM||||Tread pattern is the primary factor in determining how the tire handles rain.  Different tires would be your best bet.  However, you can help your situation by inflating your tires to the maximum recommended psi indicated on the tire sidewall.  Any tire will hydroplane at nine times the square root of the tire pressure.  So, the higher the pressure, the higher the hydoplaning speed.  However, this will effect ride quality and tire wear. 
